i.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119693","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119693","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119693.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119693.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Setting a property on a `PlaceHolderScriptInstance` (e.g. editor scripts without `@tool`) causes a segfault when the assigned value's type differs from the property's declared type and the value is later accessed through a validated builtin method call. This causes the incoming type data to be cast as the declared type and crashes when invoking the method.\r\n\r\nConvert the incoming value to the property's declared type when a strict conversion is available, matching what `GDScriptInstance::set()` already does.\r\n\r\nFixes #115469","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119693/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119693/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}